     a bespoke toggle (specimen on /brand). It is a native `<details>`, so
     keyboard and screen-reader support are inherent, and `interactions.css`
     already rotates `.delta-chevron` off the `[open]` attribute with no script. */
  /* Collapsed, the control is a bar holding four words, so it takes the prose
     measure of the paragraph above it rather than the full container. Opening
     releases it to the width its grid needs, and `max-width` is transitioned so
     that release reads as the panel widening rather than as a jump.

     Below the measure the viewport is already narrower than 800px, so both
     states render identically and no breakpoint override is needed. */
  .mcp-disclosure {
    max-width: var(--mcp-measure);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    transition: max-width var(--transition-slow);
  }

  .mcp-disclosure[open] {
